  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0518' consists of seven tables.\nThe 'Maze' table holds information about the maze files and their associated IDs. It includes columns for the Maze_File_Path, Maze_ID, and Maze_Name.\nThe 'User' table stores user-related information. It includes columns for Contact_Information, Name, and User_ID.\nThe 'Robot' table contains information about the robots. It includes columns for Current_Position, Maze_ID, Robot_ID, Robot_Type, and Timer_Status. The Maze_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Maze table.\nThe 'Forward_Sensor' table holds information about the forward sensors. It includes columns for Front_Status, Left_Status, Right_Status, Robot_ID, and Sensor_ID. The Robot_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Robot table.\nThe 'Proximity_Sensor' table contains information about the proximity sensors. It includes columns for Coin_Status, Ghost_Status, Robot_ID, and Sensor_ID. The Robot_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Robot table.\nThe 'Timer' table stores information about the timers. It includes columns for Robot_ID, Timer_Event_Description, Timer_Event_Time, and Timer_ID. The Robot_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Robot table.\nFinally, the 'User_Robot_Operation' table logs operations performed by users on the robots. It includes columns for Operation_Time, Operation_Type, Robot_ID, and User_ID. Both Robot_ID and User_ID are foreign keys referencing the Robot and User tables respectively. The combination of Robot_ID and User_ID forms the primary key of this table, ensuring entity integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements:\n1.Maze: Each maze needs to record its basic information, including Maze ID, Maze Name, and Maze File Path.\n2.Robot: Each robot needs to record its basic information, including Robot ID, Robot Type, Current Position, Timer Status, and Maze ID. Robot ID is the unique identifier for each robot, and Maze ID is a Foreign key pointing to the Maze ID in the Maze table.\n3.Forward Sensor: Each forward sensor needs to record its basic information, including Sensor ID, Robot ID, Left Status, Right Status, and Front Status.\n4.Proximity Sensor: Each proximity sensor needs to record its basic information, including Sensor ID, Robot ID, Coin Status, and Ghost Status.\n5.Timer: Each timer needs to record its basic information, including Timer ID, Robot ID, Timer Event Description, and Timer Event Time.\n6.User: Each user needs to record their basic information, including User ID, Name, and Contact Information.\n7.User Robot Operation: Each user can perform operations on a robot. This operation records User ID, Operation Type, Operation Time, and Robot ID.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0518.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0518\nCREATE TABLE `maze` (\n  `maze_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `maze_file_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `maze_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`maze_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `robot` (\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `robot_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `current_position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `timer_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `maze_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`robot_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `robot_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`maze_id`) REFERENCES `maze` (`maze_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `forward_sensor` (\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `front_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `left_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `right_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sensor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `forward_sensor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `proximity_sensor` (\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `coin_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `ghost_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sensor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `proximity_sensor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `timer` (\n  `timer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `timer_event_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `timer_event_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`timer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `timer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_robot_operation` (\n  `robot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`robot_id`, `user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_robot_operation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`robot_id`) REFERENCES `robot` (`robot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_robot_operation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
